      "text": "To solve the given expression, we need to identify the pattern and then sum the positive and negative terms separately.\n\nThe given expression is:\n\\[\n1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\n\\]\n\nFirst, observe the sequence of terms. The sequence alternates between positive and negative terms. The sequence of positive terms is \\(1, 7, 13, \\ldots, 55\\), and the sequence of negative terms is \\(-4, -10, -16, \\ldots, -52\\).\n\nThe positive terms form an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a_1 = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\). To find the number of terms in this sequence, we use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:\n\\[\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n\\]\nSetting \\(a_n = 55\\):\n\\[\n55 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\n\\]\n\\[\n55 = 1 + 6n - 6\n\\]\n\\[\n55 = 6n - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n60 = 6n\n\\]\n\\[\nn = 10\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 10 positive terms.\n\nNext, the negative terms form an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a_1 = -4\\) and the common difference \\(d = -6\\). The last term is \\(-52\\). The number of terms in this sequence is also 10, so there are also 10 negative terms.\n\nNow, calculate the sum of the positive terms:\n\\[\nS_{\\text{positive}} = \\frac{n}{2} (2a_1 + (n-1)d)\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(n = 10\\), \\(a_1 = 1\\), and \\(d = 6\\):\n\\[\nS_{\\text{positive}} = \\frac{10}{2} (2 \\cdot 1 + (10-1) \\cdot 6)\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{positive}} = 5 (2 + 9 \\cdot 6)\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{positive}} = 5 (2 + 54)\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{positive}} = 5 \\cdot 56\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{positive}} = 280\n\\]\n\nCalculate the sum of the negative terms:\n\\[\nS_{\\text{negative}} = \\frac{n}{2} (2a_1 + (n-1)d)\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(n = 10\\), \\(a_1 = -4\\), and \\(d = -6\\):\n\\[\nS_{\\text{negative}} = \\frac{10}{2} (2 \\cdot -4 + (10-1) \\cdot -6)\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{negative}} = 5 (-8 + 9 \\cdot -6)\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{negative}} = 5 (-8 - 54)\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{negative}} = 5 \\cdot -62\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{negative}} = -310\n\\]\n\nFinally, the total sum of the expression is:\n\\[\nS_{\\text{total}} = S_{\\text{positive}} - S_{\\text{negative}}\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{total}} = 280 - (-310)\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{total}} = 280 + 310\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{\\text{total}} = 590\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{590}\n\\]",
